# Vulcan — AI Agent Instructions

This project has a **Vulcan** running locally. You can deploy interactive HTML pages to it for the user to interact with in their browser.

## When to Use

Deploy a page whenever you need to:
- Show a diff comparison for the user to review before applying
- Visualize data, charts, or dashboards
- Build an interactive UI for code review, refactoring previews, or file browsers
- Present complex information that benefits from a visual layout
- Let the user click a button to confirm/apply changes

## How to Deploy

Use `curl` or `fetch` to POST to `http://localhost:3000/api/view/deploy`:

```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/view/deploy \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"name": "my_page", "html": "<!DOCTYPE html><html>...</html>"}'
```

The server responds with the URL: `http://localhost:3000/view/my_page.html`

Then tell the user to open that URL in their browser.

## HTML Template Rules

1. **Always include bridge.js** in `<head>`:
```html
<script src="/bridge.js"></script>
```

2. **Use local libraries ONLY** (no external CDNs):
```html
<script src="/lib/tailwind.min.js"></script>    <!-- Tailwind CSS -->
<script src="/lib/echarts.min.js"></script>     <!-- ECharts -->
<script src="/lib/g6.min.js"></script>          <!-- AntV G6 -->
```

3. **Single-file HTML** — all CSS and JS must be inline.

4. **Design** — use Tailwind CSS utility classes. Make it clean, modern, responsive.

## Bridge API (window.Vulcan)

The bridge.js script injects a `window.Vulcan` object into every page. The page's JS can call:

| Method | Description | Example |
|--------|-------------|---------|
| `Vulcan.readFile(path)` | Read a local file | `await Vulcan.readFile('./src/app.ts')` |
| `Vulcan.writeFile(path, content)` | Write to a local file | `await Vulcan.writeFile('./utils.js', newCode)` |
| `Vulcan.execute(cmd, args?)` | Run a whitelisted shell command | `await Vulcan.execute('git status')` |
| `Vulcan.getProjectTree(depth?)` | Get project directory tree | `await Vulcan.getProjectTree(3)` |
| `Vulcan.getProjectInfo()` | Get project metadata | `await Vulcan.getProjectInfo()` |
| `Vulcan.toast(msg, type)` | Show notification (success/error/info) | `Vulcan.toast('Saved!', 'success')` |
| `Vulcan.deployView(name, html)` | Deploy another page | `await Vulcan.deployView('detail', html)` |

## Example: Diff View with One-Click Apply

```javascript
const html = `<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <script src="/bridge.js"></script>
  <script src="/lib/tailwind.min.js"></script>
</head>
<body class="bg-gray-900 text-white p-6 font-mono">
  <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Refactor Preview</h1>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-6">
    <div>
      <h2 class="text-red-400 mb-2">Before</h2>
      <pre class="bg-red-900/20 p-4 rounded text-sm overflow-x-auto">OLD_CODE_HERE</pre>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2 class="text-green-400 mb-2">After</h2>
      <pre class="bg-green-900/20 p-4 rounded text-sm overflow-x-auto">NEW_CODE_HERE</pre>
    </div>
  </div>
  <button onclick="apply()" class="bg-blue-600 hover:bg-blue-700 px-6 py-2 rounded-lg font-semibold">
    Apply Changes
  </button>
  <script>
    async function apply() {
      var newCode = \\\`NEW_CODE_HERE\\\`;
      await Vulcan.writeFile('./target.js', newCode);
      Vulcan.toast('Changes applied!', 'success');
      document.querySelector('button').textContent = 'Applied!';
      document.querySelector('button').disabled = true;
    }
  <\/script>
</body>
</html>`;

await fetch('http://localhost:3000/api/view/deploy', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
  body: JSON.stringify({ name: 'refactor_preview', html })
});
// Tell user: "Open http://localhost:3000/view/refactor_preview.html to review and apply."
```

## Other Useful API Endpoints

| Endpoint | Method | Purpose |
|----------|--------|---------|
| `/api/view/list` | GET | List all deployed pages |
| `/api/fs/read` | POST `{path}` | Read a local file |
| `/api/fs/write` | POST `{path, content}` | Write a local file |
| `/api/sys/exec` | POST `{cmd, args?}` | Execute whitelisted command |
| `/api/project/tree` | GET | Get project directory tree |
| `/api/project/info` | GET | Get project metadata |
| `/api/health` | GET | Check server status |

## Command Whitelist for /api/sys/exec

Only these commands are allowed (for safety):
- **git**: status, diff, log, branch, show, tag, remote, add, checkout
- **npm/yarn/pnpm**: run, test, lint, build, start
- **read-only**: ls, cat, head, tail, wc, find, grep, tree, pwd
- **dev tools**: node, python, echo, date, which, curl

## Startup (Auto-Start)

**Always check and start Vulcan automatically when needed. Never ask the user to start it manually.**

Before deploying any view, check if Vulcan is running:
```bash
curl -s http://localhost:3000/api/health
```

If it fails (connection refused), start it automatically:
```bash
vulcan start --no-open
```

Then proceed with the deployment. The page will auto-open in the Vulcan shell (browser opens to `http://localhost:3000/#view-name`).
